{
	title: 'Web disclosure controls for short and long',
	spec: `The web and the terminal switch a card between short and long the same way: Ctrl-O, /toggle and, on the web, a tap.

Web header: a small disclosure triangle before the time, pointing right when the card is short and down when it is long, turned 90 degrees with a CSS transform transition. A tap on the header or the triangle switches short and long. A tap on the body still collapses the card, until the user has tested selection and scrolling on a phone.

Web tool card: a long one shows its command and all its output. A command toggle appears only when the command was really cut (more than one line, or measured overflow in the DOM); it shows the whole command and back.

Terminal short Bash card: the command's first line, cut with '…', then the short rows of output, the same height while running and after (a whole multi-line command made a short card about 20 rows tall).`,
	status: 'done',
	notes: [
		'Web headers and body taps use folds.disclose, retaining each card’s last open state by session and block key; /collapse also preserves the configured open state. ToolCommand uses one-line CSS ellipsis and a ResizeObserver to offer Show command only for multiline details or measured horizontal overflow. Its DOM stays owned by Card while output updates. The command toggle does not change output verbosity. Structured presentations remain in long; glimpse shows the raw call and output. Terminal Bash clips the first command line but retains declared edits, non-default timeout and unfamiliar arguments below it. Updated browser tests replace the former header/body three-click cycle and cover separate command/output disclosure, width-dependent overflow, and restoring long after /collapse.',
		'Verification: ./test ran with 1550 passing and 11 failing normal tests outside this change; the new Bash glimpse test passed. ./test item-view passed all 7 tests. Final ./test-expensive web.test had 46 passing and 3 failing tests: reduced-motion Nudge timing, transcript variant setup, and foreground/background Bash expected content. The bp1 controls test and updated EDIT, background-collapse and queued-card tests passed, with no Solid diagnostics. Desktop (900 px) and phone-emulated (390 px) screenshots were reviewed, including cut and expanded commands. Scoped lint and git diff --check passed. No physical phone selection/scrolling check was available.'
	],
	needs: ['hyt'],
	foldInto: ['hyt']
}
